{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 MemoryAPI JSFX Suite\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A cross-platform collection of 15 studio mixing, mastering, and synthesis JSFX plugins for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaper.fm/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Cockos REAPER
}}}
, featuring custom hardware-accelerated vector UIs styled in the {\b Catppuccin Mocha} palette.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Installation (ReaPack)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab In REAPER, navigate to {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import repositories...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Paste the repository index URL and click {\b OK}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/memoryapi/memoryapi-jsfx/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Open {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Browse packages...}, search for {\f1 memoryapi} (or any plugin below), right-click to {\b Install}, and click {\b Apply}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Suite Architecture\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every plugin in this repository shares a unified design standard:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Cross-Platform & Native:} Runs with zero external dependencies on Linux, Windows, and macOS.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Linux X11 / HiDPI Scaling:} Built-in {\f1 100% / 125% / 150%} UI scale toggles and responsive window geometry for crisp typography on unscaled X11 and Wayland displays.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Click-Free Transport & Automation:} Full parameter exposure to REAPER automation lanes with {\f1 ext_noinit} state preservation and Cytomic Zero-Delay Feedback (ZDF) / State Variable Filter (SVF) topologies.\sa180\par}
